# Quantitative Methodology in Sociology: The Last Twenty-five Years.

**Authors:** Schuessler, Karl F.

## Abstract
Argues that recent work in research methods in sociology consists largely of adapting methods developed elsewhere (statistics, demography, economics) for answering relatively simple questions about social change. These questions reflect practical as well as theoretical concerns. Discusses social indicators, social forecasting, cohort, occupational inheritance, and panel methods. (Author/KC)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ231060

